### Canonical text-only publication foundation

On 2026-10-08, logical draft-ID commands were connected through the ordinary
CLI and admitted MCP tools to the local service. The first step requires the
exact saved revision, admits account capabilities, and durably freezes the
project/capability snapshot before journaled execution. Each call performs at
most one set/question write; caller paths and retry overrides are rejected.

Progress remains separate from publication proof. Final verification requires
completed checkpoints, no uncertain attempt, exact remote metadata/question
state, and two matching fresh observations. Unsupported media is refused before
snapshot creation or provider inspection; editing existing quizzes is not
claimed by this creation-only command family.

Targeted portable tests cover revision conflicts, concurrent duplicate steps,
uncertain outcomes/reconciliation, cancellation after journal persistence,
unsupported media, immutable bounded storage, and changed remote observations.
An integration fixture crosses real MCP, CLI subprocess, HTTP, persistence, and
