## Blockers

Text-only Add Question browser mechanics now submit once and require exact
post-submit read-back. Media upload, existing-quiz editing, and live canonical
publication acceptance remain pending. The connected legacy extension must be
replaced before the current bounded read contracts can verify a real result.

Safari, macOS, and ChatGPT-specific hardening belongs only to task blooket-15
and does not block this functional record.


On 2026-10-09, prepared-media admission began copying every byte buffer and
scalar fact before awaiting another asset read. A synthetic reusable-buffer
regression reproduces the previous drift and proves that already admitted
bytes remain unchanged. A versioned immutable media-identity model now binds
stable ID, recipe revision, format, actual byte length, and SHA-256; exact
runtime admission rejects duplicate IDs, arbitrary paths/URLs, malformed
hashes, and oversized identities.

The persisted write executor can receive that expected identity context. Any
changed bytes, revision, format, or missing required asset stop before mutation
budget reservation, the attempt journal, or a remote write. Differential
question reconciliation can use a copied admitted expected identity and requires
version-four remote byte evidence plus preservation of the prior collection.
It never resolves the current library to decide the outcome of an older write.

This is portable execution/verifier composition evidence. At this checkpoint,
canonical publication snapshots did not yet persist this context. Subsequent
version-two snapshot foundation below addresses durable identity composition;
new media creation and live publication acceptance remain pending.

The [Node Buffer documentation](https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html), checked
on 2026-10-09, distinguishes copying typed-array contents from sharing its
underlying ArrayBuffer. The implementation deliberately copies the prepared
view and hashes those exact owned bytes; a digest proves equality, not publisher
trust or provider success.


A follow-up regression reproduced caller-side expected-identity drift during
session observation: the initial implementation could accept the newly changed
bytes. Persisted execution now validates and copies expected identities at
entry,
before lock acquisition or session I/O. A malformed context cannot be ignored
when no media resolver is supplied, and neither failure opens an attempt journal
or dispatches a write. The synthetic regressions fail against the prior commit
and pass with this entry-boundary correction.

### Durable expected-media snapshot foundation (2026-10-09)

Canonical publication now writes an exact version-two frozen snapshot, with an
empty identity context for currently admitted text drafts. Version-one text
snapshots still resume with identical plan/checkpoint/journal bindings. The
shared decoder admits exact question-image identities without descriptive
metadata or fabricated paths and rejects unverifiable covers and answer images.

For media plans, sorted ID, recipe revision, format, actual length, and SHA-256
join the desired-state hash. Changing those facts cannot reinterpret an old
checkpoint or attempt. Reconciliation and final verification use the frozen
context; they never fetch current local bytes to decide an old remote outcome.
The owning service now passes its existing prepared-media port and decoded
expected context into persisted execution.

Portable regressions verify legacy resumption, identity-order independence,
changed-byte plan binding, malformed/extra/missing identities, capability
refusals, simulated interrupted image reconciliation, and final image conflict.
The simulated provider is explicitly not live canonical acceptance. New and
resumed media mutations remain closed; initial media capture, corrected native
upload acceptance, and real CLI/MCP publication remain required.
